  "notes": "The Enterprise Campus 24S spec table prints no PoE row: Port Layout \"1 GbE RJ45 1 (1G/100M/10M), 2.5 GbE RJ45 8 (2.5G/1G/100M/10M), 10 GbE RJ45 16 (10G/5G/2.5G/1G/100M/10M), 25G SFP28 4 (25G/10G/1G), 100G QSFP28 2 (100G), Console 1\", Max. Power Consumption 150W, Power Supply \"(2) Hot-swappable AC/DC 550W power modules\". The one \"Power Output\" row on the sheet sits under **LEDs**, next to Ethernet and SFP28 - it names a status lamp, not a PSE port. The PoE member is a separate model (ecs-24s-poe.json) with its own budget. Without `poeIn: false` all 25 copper sockets each asked for 12.95 W - **323.7 W**."
